Create a graph of mining sites and candidate connections.
Choose a starting site and add it to the network.
Place its outgoing edges in a minimum-priority queue.
Repeatedly select the lowest-cost edge that connects a site in the network to a site outside it.
Add that edge and new site to the network; add the new site’s eligible edges to the queue.
Continue until all sites are connected or no eligible edges remain.
Display the selected edges and their total cost. If some sites remain disconnected, report that no complete network is possible.
